    "note": "Three protections at three speeds. The firmware trips on current at 8 A, which is above the 5.5 A a synchronised move draws and below the 10.2 A a jam draws, so a jam is caught inside a control period and an ordinary movement is not. It trips on temperature at 85 C, which catches sustained current above the 6.4 A the board can carry indefinitely. The 15 A fuse protects the wiring from a short and nothing else, because a fuse that opens drops a limb and cannot be reset by software."
